  "body": "**Blocked by:** #225, #113\n\n## Context\n\nIssue #225 formalized the unit and real-PostgreSQL integration tiers with stable scripts. This part completes the three-tier toolset with the third, smallest tier: a named e2e harness for the riskiest cross-module flows, with one representative scenario rather than complete coverage. It reuses the ephemeral PostgreSQL lifecycle from #225. #115 and later batches add scenarios to this harness as they introduce cross-module flows.\n\n## Task\n\n- Add a named e2e harness (its own Vitest configuration and include pattern, clearly distinguished from the unit and integration tiers) that boots the relevant modules through `ModuleRegistry` (#108) and the public contracts they expose, against the ephemeral PostgreSQL lifecycle from #225.\n- Add one representative cross-module scenario that crosses a module boundary only through public contracts (registry projections, the choke point, or registered queue tasks) — never through a module's private internals.\n- Extend the local scripts from #225 so the e2e tier runs alone and so that all three tiers run together, with isolated setup/teardown.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- E2E harness configuration, the representative scenario, and the scripts.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- The unit and integration tiers (#225).\n- Complete e2e coverage for every module, mocked-DB substitutes, and CI workflow files.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- All three suites run independently and together.\n- The representative e2e crosses a module boundary through public contracts and passes against real PostgreSQL.\n",
